{% macro explorer_rules(target) %}
- **Narrow, not broad.** A broadly scoped explorer misses, mistakes and
  invents details. At most three related questions each; three disjoint
  questions are three explorers. A broad orienting survey is a fine *first*
  step, but nothing in it can be relied on: ground-truth every detail you
  build on through a narrow follow-up.
- **Serial, never parallel**, even for disjoint questions. Launch one, wait,
  read its report, let it sharpen the next question.
- Each explorer writes its own {{ target }};
  give it that path and read the file — its reply is only its status line.
{%- endmacro %}
